      "prompt_tokens": 25,
      "completion_tokens": 1043,
      "output": "\n\nWater is a chemical substance with the molecular formula **H₂O**, consisting of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom. It is a fundamental component of life and one of the most abundant and unique substances on Earth. Here's a breakdown of its key characteristics:\n\n### **Chemical Composition**\n- **Molecular Structure**: A water molecule is polar, with a bent shape due to the unequal sharing of electrons between oxygen and hydrogen. This polarity allows water to form **hydrogen bonds**, which influence its physical and chemical properties.\n\n### **Physical Properties**\n- **States of Matter**: Water exists as a **liquid** at standard temperature and pressure, but it can also transition into **solid (ice)** when frozen and **gas (water vapor)** when heated. \n- **Unique Properties**: \n  - **High Specific Heat**: It absorbs and releases heat slowly, helping regulate temperature in organisms and environments.\n  - **Cohesion & Adhesion**: Molecules stick to each other (cohesion) and to other surfaces (adhesion), enabling processes like capillary action in plants.\n  - **Low Density as Ice**: Ice floats because hydrogen bonds form a crystalline structure, making it less dense than liquid water.\n\n### **Biological Importance**\n- **Essential for Life**: All known living organisms require water for survival. It acts as a **solvent** for biochemical reactions, transports nutrients, and maintains cell structure.\n- **Human Body**: Composes about 60% of the human body, aiding in digestion, temperature regulation, and waste removal.\n\n### **Environmental Role**\n- **Hydrological Cycle**: Water cycles through evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and runoff, shaping weather, ecosystems, and landscapes.\n- **Ecosystem Support**: Sustains aquatic and terrestrial life, influences climate, and shapes geological features through erosion and sediment transport.\n\n### **Other Key Traits**\n- **Universal Solvent**: Dissolves more substances than any other liquid, facilitating chemical reactions in biological and environmental systems.\n- **Transparency and Purity**: Naturally clear, tasteless, and odorless, though it can contain dissolved minerals or impurities.\n\nIn summary, water is a versatile, life-sustaining substance with properties that make it indispensable for biological processes, environmental stability, and human survival. Its unique molecular behavior underpins its critical roles in nature and technology."
